# Citation metadata for the scoRch.generator R package (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# The software release and the study's processed dataset are separate records:
#   software: this repository, version 1.0.0, released on 12 October 2026
#             (the Zenodo software DOI is added under `identifiers:` once the
#             release is archived; see docs/release_checklist.md)
#   dataset:  "Processed ERA5 daily maximum temperature data for SCORCH,
#             1940-2025", version 1.0.0, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21717874
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use scoRch.generator, please cite the software and the study it
  implements. When you use the study's results, also cite the processed
  dataset (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21717874).
type: software
title: "scoRch.generator: Spatiotemporal Classification of Regional Compound Heatwaves"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/fawazbouhamad/scoRch.generator"
url: "https://github.com/fawazbouhamad/scoRch.generator"
abstract: >-
  R implementation of SCORCH, the method of Bouhamad and Najibi for finding
  regionally extensive compound heatwaves in gridded daily maximum
  temperature: local heatwaves at every grid cell, regionally extensive days,
  DBSCAN clusters of heatwave cells, principal-component ellipses with
  temperature-weighted centroids, four compound-event types, and power-law
  and log-Gaussian Cox process models. One configuration file and one
  function run the complete workflow on ERA5 or prepared daily maximum
  temperature; the package reproduces the catalogs, tables and model results
  of the study from its archived input.
keywords:
  - compound heatwaves
  - heatwave typology
  - spatiotemporal clustering
  - DBSCAN
  - principal-component ellipses
  - log-Gaussian Cox process
  - ERA5 reanalysis
  - R package
authors:
